# 🔐 Cyber Data Cleaning & Visualization Project

## 📌 Overview

This project focuses on cleaning and analyzing a cybersecurity dataset to extract meaningful insights. The goal is to understand data quality, identify patterns, and visualize key features.

---

## 🧰 Tools & Technologies

* Python
* Pandas
* NumPy
* Matplotlib
* Seaborn
* Jupyter Notebook

---

## 🧹 Data Cleaning Steps

* Removed duplicate records
* Handled missing values
* Dropped irrelevant features (time-based columns with no variation)
* Selected appropriate data types for analysis

---

## 📊 Data Visualization

* Severity distribution using count plots
* Abuse confidence score distribution using histograms
* Top IP address frequency analysis
* Boxplots for numeric feature overview

---

## 🧠 Key Insights

* Dataset shows very low variance in numeric features
* Severity remains constant across all records
* Abuse confidence score is consistently high (~100)
* No IP address repetition, indicating lack of frequency patterns
* Time-related features were removed due to no variation

---

## ⚠️ Conclusion

The dataset lacks diversity and is not suitable for predictive modeling without additional data or feature engineering. However, it serves as a good example for data cleaning and exploratory analysis.

---

## 🚀 Future Work

* Apply feature engineering techniques
* Use a more diverse dataset for machine learning
* Build classification models for attack detection

---

